<% set_meta_tags title: "Launching the partnership between Bleau.info and Boolder" %>

<main class="bg-white px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 sm:py-16 lg:px-8">
  <article class="prose prose-emerald prose-lg mx-auto" lang="en">
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl">Launching the partnership between Bleau.info and Boolder</h1>

    <p class="text-gray-500"><time datetime="2026-10-30">30 October 2026</time> by Nicolas</p>

    <%= image_tag "banner-bleau-info-partnership.png", alt: "Boolder × Bleau.info", class: "w-full rounded-lg" %>

    <p>Since 2021, Boolder has been working to build the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.boolder.com/en/app">best climbing guide app for Fontainebleau</a>.</p>

    <p>Our goal is to help climbers find their way around the forest and discover boulders suited to their level.</p>

    <p>We are proud to have helped more than 100,000 people <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.boolder.com/en/fontainebleau">discover</a> (or rediscover) thousands of boulders scattered across the 22,000 hectares of Fontainebleau forest.</p>

    <p>Thanks to the passion and spare time of a team of <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.boolder.com/en/about">volunteers</a>, the app has remained free and open-source.</p>

    <p>Today, we are joining forces with Bleau.info.</p>

    <h2>Bleau.info, the bible of Fontainebleau</h2>

    <p>Thanks to <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://bleau.info/profiles/bart.van.raaij">Bart van Raaij</a> and many <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://bleau.info/about">contributors</a>, Bleau.info has meticulously catalogued more than 40,000 boulder problems over the years, with grades, descriptions, photos, videos, beta and more.</p>

    <p>A monumental effort, celebrated by the climbing community and freely available on the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="http://bleau.info/">Bleau.info</a> website.</p>

    <p>Bleau.info has naturally established itself as the go-to reference for climbing in Fontainebleau, earning the trust of the entire community.</p>

    <p>Unfortunately, keeping everything free and relying entirely on volunteers is becoming harder to sustain, while climbing’s popularity and visitor numbers in the forest continue to grow.</p>

    <p>How can we keep this going sustainably for the next 25 years?</p>

    <h2>A partnership between Bleau.info and Boolder</h2>

    <p>Today, we are launching a paid offering together.</p>

    <p>Here is what that means:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>Bleau.info remains free</li>
      <li>Boolder moves to a paid subscription at €15 per year</li>
      <li>The money raised is split equally between Bleau.info and Boolder.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>You get the best climbing guide to Fontainebleau while supporting both our projects for years to come.</p>

    <p>The revenue will allow us to provide more frequent updates.</p>

    <p>We are also keeping several areas free for anyone who wants to discover the joy of climbing in Fontainebleau without committing to a subscription.</p>

    <h2>A gradual transition</h2>

    <p>We are a small team of passionate climbers, and we will need time (and your patience!) to bring this partnership to life over the coming months.</p>

    <p>Please forgive us if we make mistakes along the way, and feel free to <a href="/en/about#contact" target="_blank" rel="noopener">contact us</a> with your questions, feedback or concerns.</p>

    <p>One thing is certain: this partnership fills us with optimism.</p>

    <p>We hope it will help secure the future of Bleau.info and Boolder, while preserving each project’s mission and independence.</p>

    <p>Happy climbing!</p>

    <p>Émile and Nicolas.</p>

